From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:16:54 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-glymur: Keep the PCIe 0 tunnel domain on for a
 device on the wakeup path

USB4 host router 0 holds the power domain of the PCIe root complex it
tunnels into while it runs, as router 1 does and as the platform's
firmware tables list it for both, and is kept across system sleep with
its domains on the wakeup path. Let genpd leave that domain on for
such a device, as it already does for router 1's.

Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5.2
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-glymur.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-glymur.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-glymur.c
index 88871445c..7c4ec3391 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-glymur.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-glymur.c
@@ -7482,6 +7482,7 @@ static struct gdsc gcc_pcie_0_tunnel_gdsc = {
 	.clk_dis_wait_val = 0xf,
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "gcc_pcie_0_tunnel_gdsc",
+		.flags = GENPD_FLAG_ACTIVE_WAKEUP,
 	},
 	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
 	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE | VOTABLE,
-- 
2.56.1

